@* HelpChecklistPage: help topic "Checklist" at "/help/checklist". Static text and screenshots. *@
@page "/help/checklist"

<HelpTopicFrame Slug="checklist">
    <section class="card">
        <p>Every review has a checklist of checks grouped in sections. Answer each check <strong>Pass</strong>,
            <strong>Fail</strong> or <strong>N/A</strong>. A Fail or N/A needs a short justification. A section that
            does not apply to the review can be switched off, with a reason.</p>
        <p>You answer in the ballot of your reviewer slot. If you are not a reviewer yet, press <strong>Assign me as
            reviewer</strong> on the checklist: it adds you as a new reviewer of the review. With one slot your
            answers count at once. With several slots they are a draft until you press <strong>Submit
            ballot</strong>, or <strong>Submit and sign</strong> to hand in your ballot and sign in one step.</p>
        <p>With several reviewers, everyone answers on their own first: you see the other reviewers' answers, the dispute
            counts and the conclusion only after you hand in your own ballot. You always see who has handed in. The
            lead of the review, administrators and Auditors see the others at once, and so does everyone in a review
            with a single reviewer slot or in a concluded review. Once you may see them, a check on which the reviewers
            differ shows their answers side by side, for example <em>Alice: Pass /
            Bob: N/A</em>, with the reason each of the others wrote, and a <strong>Discuss</strong> button that starts a
            discussion about that check. At the top of the checklist a line counts the checks the reviewers answered
            differently (<em>1 check answered differently. Open it to discuss.</em>). The ballots line says who has
            not handed in yet (<em>1 of 2 ballots handed in. Bob has not handed in yet.</em>), and when you can sign
            before everyone has, a caution above <strong>Submit and sign</strong> names them.
            The discussion is a <strong>Question</strong> unless you choose <strong>Finding (goes in the
            report)</strong>.</p>
        <p>A Fail answer does not block signing. When the submitted ballots agree on a Fail, the agreed outcome is
            <strong>Rejected</strong> (provisional until every slot has signed), the status line reads <em>Checklist
            complete, 1 check failed.</em>, and a conclusion that states the
            reasons is needed before it can be signed. See
            <a href="/help/reviewers-and-signing">Reviewers and signing</a>.</p>
        <p>In a follow-up review, answers carried over from the earlier review are marked <strong>Carried
            from</strong> with a link to that review. A check that failed in the earlier review shows that Fail
            read-only until you decide it again.</p>
        <figure class="help-figure">
            <img class="help-shot" src="/help/checklist-1.png" loading="lazy"
                 alt="The Checklist page with the progress summary, the Next unanswered check button and the first section with Pass, Fail and N/A buttons." />
            <figcaption>The checklist of a review.</figcaption>
        </figure>
    </section>
</HelpTopicFrame>
